, the cause is more likely market-wide or in the underlying assets than specific to this fund.\n\nThen examine underlying trading frictions, such as holdings liquidity, settlement timing, and creation/redemption constraints.\n\nFinally, review AP and market-maker participation: creation and redemption activity, quoting behavior, and whether capacity or credit limits are binding.\n\nCorrective options, scaled to the findings, could include:\n- Revising fair-value or pricing policies\n- Engaging APs and market makers\n- Adjusting creation baskets or in-kind mechanics\n- Enhancing investor disclosure\n- Updating liquidity risk management\n\nThe board should document its findings and reasoning before concluding that arbitrage has failed.","ttft_ms":2646,"type":"result","duration_ms":4121,"uuid":"5bda7d92-d382-4860-9159-e9c1eee2c964","ttft_stream_ms":431,"time_to_request_ms":67,"first_content_frame_ms":431,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
